@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print` and :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log`. It converts its positional objects to strings, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("foo", "bar", sep=".", end="!\n")
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers, does not word wrap or crop the text, does not interpret :ref:`console_markup`, and does not replace emoji codes. Use it when you want the text written as-is.
+
+It does apply highlighting and a basic ``style``. Highlighting is on by default (``highlight=True``), so it is applied even if the Console was created with highlighting disabled. Pass ``highlight=None`` to use the Console's own setting, or ``highlight=False`` to turn highlighting off.
+
+
